# Understanding Data 

#### Data is all around us, shaping the world we live in. Whether it's the number of steps we take, the likes on a social media post, or the weather forecast. 

#### Everything can be quantified and analyzed to reveal patterns and insights that drive our decisions and innovations.

<br>

#### 🔎 **Think About** 
#### Look at the pizza party in this picture: *Can you identify where data might be hiding?  How do these everyday details turn into data that tells a story?*
<br>

<img src="https://images.code.org/7b4efe41391189f72375b8f15ba9a7e6-image-1724252501466.png" alt="design process graph of the cycle" width="70%" style="border: 2px solid black; border-radius: 8px; display: block; margin: auto; width: 70%;">

<br>

#### You might have noticed the following data:
- #### Number of people
- #### Number of adults vs. students
- #### Number of pizzas
- #### Types of pizzas
- #### Set at a school

#### There might have been data you chose to ignore, like: 
- #### Number of post-it notes 
- #### Number of blue shirts

#### You may have come to the conclusion that there is a pizza party at a school celebrating something. 


<div style="background-color: #a6e3e8; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;">

<p style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 18px; "><strong>Teacher Tip:</strong> This beginning exercise allows you to pre-assess what students know about data and to get them thinking and talking about what data is and how to analyze it.  
</p>
</div>


